{
  "about": "Hand-labelled /step cases for scripts/eval_fill_decisions.py. Synthetic: no real applicant data. Candidates are written the way content/fill-core.js's stepState describes moves. `expected` lists the right moves (\"give_up\" when stopping is right; an abstain is always read as give_up). A click on an option that does not state the fact is a WRONG CLICK unless the case lists it in `harmless` (e.g. \"Not in List\"); a group open and every other move is wrong-but-harmless when it is not expected.",
